WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
These overcomers who have made themselves ready—

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
what do they become?

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.500 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The bride of Christ.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The bridegroom, then, takes the bride.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
John chapter three states clearly:

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.500 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
He who has the bride is the bridegroom.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
He must increase,

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
but I must decrease.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
We can see that the bride is the increase of the
bridegroom.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
In other words, the bride is nothing else.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Strictly speaking, the bride is not a separate
person.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
What is the bride?

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The increase of the bridegroom.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
You may ask, Is that going too far?

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
What is the bride?

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.500 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The increase of the bridegroom.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The Song of Songs the brother just read with us

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
expresses this same thought.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
When we reach chapter six of the Song of Songs,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
we find this beloved.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the earlier chapters, we cannot find her name.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
I do not know about you,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
but when I read the Song of Songs as a younger man,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
I wondered if I had misread it.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Had I accidentally missed something?

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Why could I not find out her name?

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Chapter one? No. Chapter two? No.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
No name in chapters three, four, or five either.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
She is simply called the beloved.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
No name at all.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Then, in chapter six, a name suddenly appears. What
is it?

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shulammite.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.500 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Actually, the word woman is an addition in the
Chinese translation.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
It is simply Shulammite.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shulammite is the feminine form of Solomon.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:48.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
In other words, this beloved is a female Solomon.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.500 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
You see, the revelation in the Bible is consistent.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Who is the bride?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The increase of the bridegroom.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The bride is not a separate person.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
She is, in essence, the increase of the bridegroom.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Who is the bride?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
The bride is the Shulammite,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
a female Solomon.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.750 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
To attain this,

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.500 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
we come to the third point:

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
maturity.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the third point we read the word maturity.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
What does the original Greek word mean?

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.250 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Reaching the goal.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.000 line:72% position:50% align:center size:92%
Brothers and sisters, I hope you will seriously
enter into this point.
